//==
// # Coincident vertex pairs on a grid: types (complexity sweep, chunk V7, TKT-375)
//
// The cell of the tolerance grid CoincidentVertexPairsGridded buckets vertices into
// (mesh-coincident-gridded.library.plato).

// The cell of a uniform grid holding a point: the floors of the point's coordinates divided by
// the cell side. The coordinates are whole Numbers, not Integers, so a model far from the origin
// or a tolerance far below its extent cannot overflow a 32-bit key; cells compare
// lexicographically (CoincidenceCellAtMost).
// Invariant: X, Y and Z are whole numbers of magnitude below CoincidenceCellBound wherever the
// grid is used (IsExactCoincidenceCell).
type CoincidenceCell
    implements IValue
{
    X: Number;
    Y: Number;
    Z: Number;
}
